//! Readings keyed by the typing ENVIRONMENT (`Trust.Protocol.Seal`): a chain
//! of 640 generic fns, each sorting a copy of its `Vec` and calling the next
//! (their parameters named `T` and `U` in turn), called once at `u8`. Each body
//! is read once where it stands, and what it names at its parameters is the
//! same question in every fn of the chain, read once. The seal HOLDS. Review 4
//! of the review-14 build found the readings keyed by the fn whose parameters
//! they name: each fn was read once for every fn above it, N^2/2 times, and
//! this program was refused at the bound of 2,000,000 instances. The twin
//! (`_readings.rs`) swaps two holders at the end of such a chain.

#![allow(unused)]

pub struct Cell { n: u32 }
impl Cell {
    fn new() -> Self { Cell { n: 0 } }
    fn bump(&mut self) { self.n += 1; }
}
pub struct App { cell: Cell, k: u8 }
impl App { fn new() -> Self { App { cell: Cell::new(), k: 0 } } }
